  "result": "Excellent! All 104 tests pass. I've successfully implemented customer ID normalization. Here's what was added:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**src/customers.js**\n- Added `normalizeId(id)` function that:\n  - Trims leading/trailing whitespace\n  - Converts to uppercase\n- Updated `getCustomer()` to normalize the ID before lookup\n\n**src/invoices.js**\n- Imported `normalizeId` from customers.js\n- Updated `createInvoice()` to:\n  - Normalize customer ID at the start of the function\n  - Use normalized ID for customer validation\n  - Store the normalized ID in the returned invoice\n- Updated `addLine()` to normalize customer ID when looking up customer for tier discounts\n\n**test/customers.test.js**\n- Imported `normalizeId`\n- Added 5 new tests:\n  - `normalizeId()` trims whitespace\n  - `normalizeId()` converts to uppercase\n  - `getCustomer()` finds customer with lowercase ID\n  - `getCustomer()` finds customer with whitespace\n  - `getCustomer()` finds customer with mixed case and whitespace\n\n**test/invoices.test.js**\n- Added 3 new tests:\n  - `createInvoice()` accepts lowercase customer ID and normalizes it\n  - `createInvoice()` accepts customer ID with trailing whitespace\n  - `createInvoice()` accepts mixed case and whitespace customer ID\n  - All verify that the returned invoice has the normalized customer ID\n\nNow the system robustly handles customer IDs from various sources (external systems, manual entry, etc.) that may have inconsistent casing or whitespace, automatically normalizing them to the canonical uppercase format stored in the customer database.",
